{"body":"## Finding\n\nRecorder first real role dogfood during issue #15 exposed a production-envelope compatibility defect. A current Pi `--mode json` stream represents one accepted terminating call twice:\n\n1. `tool_execution_end`\n2. `message_end` carrying the corresponding `toolResult`\n\n`src/recorder/extract.ts` flattens both supported representations into two `terminal` lifecycle events. `bindAcceptedLifecycle` accepts the first and rejects the state on the second, so the completed Recorder docket records:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"child\": { \"status\": \"exited\", \"exitCode\": 0 },\n  \"recorder\": { \"status\": \"completed\" },\n  \"receipt\": null,\n  \"auditObservation\": null\n}\n```\n\nNo Receipt was synthesized. Raw diagnostic streams were deleted after structural counting.\n\n## Durable evidence\n\nIssue #15 branch/docket:\n\n- `.ak/dockets/issues/15/authority/judge-003/manifest.json`\n- `.ak/dockets/issues/15/authority/judge-003/receipt-null-disposition.json`\n\nStructural replay against the real envelope reported:\n\n```text\nrows: 1427\nissued ak_judge_output: 1\nstart ak_judge_output: 1\nterminal ak_judge_output: 2\nextracted receipt: null\n```\n\nThe two terminals had the same tool name and call ID. No semantic session payload is retained.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nEquivalent representations of the same single package acceptance in one supported machine envelope should canonicalize to one lifecycle terminal. Genuinely duplicated, replayed, conflicting, out-of-order, or mismatched terminals must still fail closed.\n\n## Required design questions\n\n- canonicalize envelope rows before lifecycle binding, or make binding representation-aware without weakening replay rejection;\n- identify equivalence with enough fields to reject conflicting duplicates;\n- add a production-shaped combined `tool_execution_end` + `message_end` regression for Judge/Reviewer and preserve existing duplicate-terminal counterexamples;\n- verify Recorder still extracts the typed Receipt/audit observation from current Pi output;\n- no change to role Souls, orchestration, migration logic, or absent-Receipt law.\n\n## Scope disposition\n\nDo **not** repair this inside issue #15 Case-A legacy migration. #15 continues through the established direct Pi typed-Receipt archival path; Recorder may still wrap the actual non-role migration command, where absence of a role Receipt is lawful.\n","state":"OPEN","title":"Recorder rejects real Pi JSON envelope that duplicates one terminal across event representations","url":"https://github.com/Akagilnc/ak-pi-workflow-roles/issues/16"}
